<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Isthmus of Panama</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Isthmus of Darién</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Isthmus of Panama is the narrow strip of land between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> Sea and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-ocean">Pacific Ocean</a> that links North and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasco-nunez-de-balboa">Vasco Núñez de Balboa</a> crossed it in 1513, and it became a key route for Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>'s Darien scheme tried to found a colony there in 1698–1700 and failed disastrously, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panama-canal">Panama Canal</a> was opened across it in 1914.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/isthmus-of-panama.jpg" alt="Isthmus of Panama" width="320" height="259" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IsthmusOfPanama.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
